# The workspace is generated output and stays out of the repo — except for
# baselines. A baseline is the reference a run is judged against, so it has to
# be committed: with nothing to compare to, CI captures a baseline from the
# commit under test and compares it against itself, and the check can never
# fail. Ignoring the contents rather than the directory itself is what lets the
# negation below apply — git cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is
# excluded. Use the "Generate Baselines" workflow to produce baselines that
# match what a Linux runner renders.
.visual-regression/*
!.visual-regression/baselines/
.visual-regression/baselines/**/versions/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.tmp_ai_studio_review/
.tmp_figma_review/
.vscode/
scratch/
dashboard_frontend/node_modules/
dashboard_frontend/dist/
dashboard_frontend/test-results/
dashboard_frontend/playwright-report/
dashboard_frontend/.env
dashboard_frontend/.env.local
dashboard_frontend/.env.*.local
.env
.env.local
*.zip
*.bak
storage.db
storage.db-shm
storage.db-wal

.idea/
